\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Bastankhah.} Alternative view of the cross-section data (\emph  {constrained, identical-copy neighbor farm}---not the unconstrained greedy upper bound): peak regret over the elliptical-rose shape space $(a, f)$ at four fixed minimum buffer distances ($K = 2000$, FunWake schedule). Real-site fits overlaid as labelled markers. Hot corner (high concentration $a$ + high folding $f$, i.e.\ concentrated unidirectional) shrinks with buffer; operational North Sea sites sit in the cool moderate-shape region for all buffer choices.}}{19}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
